    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `initials` field needed to appear on the Owner JSON response (`$.initials` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"` for firstName `john`, lastName `smith`). Following the exact pattern already used for `displayName`, I made two small changes:\n\n1. **`Person.java`** \u2014 added a `getInitials()` transient method alongside the existing `getDisplayName()`. Since `Owner` extends `Person`, both entities inherit it, and it lives on the domain object where name-derived formatting belongs:\n   ```java\n   @Transient\n   public String getInitials() {\n       return Character.toUpperCase(this.firstName.charAt(0)) + \".\"\n           + Character.toUpperCase(this.lastName.charAt(0)) + \".\";\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema, mirroring `displayName`. The code generator produces the DTO field and MapStruct auto-maps it from `getInitials()` (same convention that already wires up `displayName`), so no mapper changes were required.\n\nNo new class or catch-all was introduced \u2014 the logic reuses the established transient-getter + read-only-schema-property pattern.",
